.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fine structure of the kinetochore in the Indian muntjac</article-title><source>Exp. Cell Res.</source><volume>67</volume><year>1971</year><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5569205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ComingsandOkada1972"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Comings</surname><given-names>D.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Okada</surname><given-names>T.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Holocentric chromosomes in <italic>Oncopeltus</italic>kinetochore plates are present in mitosis but absent in meiosis</article-title><source>Chromosoma.</source><volume>37</volume><year>1972</year><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5043259</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Davisetal1983"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>F.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsao</surname><given-names>T.Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fowler</surname><given-names>S.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>P.N.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Monoclonal antibodies to mitotic cells</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>80</volume><year>1983</year><fpage>2926</fpage><lpage>2930</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6574461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Deppeetal1978"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deppe</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schierenberg</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Krieg</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoder</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name><name><surnam